.claude/settings.json:5:  "_sandbox_comment": "PLAN-136 W3 S4b: OS-level Bash containment composed into the LIVE dogfood install (no longer SPOF fail-open — the env-layer sandbox sits UNDER the hook rail and does NOT fail open). Values copied from templates/settings/settings.stack.sandbox.json (PLAN-135 W2 / S4). enabled=true contains each Bash tool-call; allowUnixSockets keeps local IPC (audit filelock, git local sockets); filesystem.writablePaths scopes writes to the repo tree + scratch ($CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR, /tmp, /var/folders), HOME stays non-writable (startup-file class); network.defaultPosture=deny with allowedDomains = the PLAN-133 egress SoT (_lib/egress_taxonomy.py _PAIR_RAIL_HOST_SUFFIXES) + operationally-required hosts. autoAllowBashIfSandboxed SHIPPED FALSE (a fail-open hook + auto-allow makes allowedDomains the SOLE exfil control — deliberate adopter choice only).",
.claude/settings.json:50:    "_credentials_comment": "PLAN-153 wave-backlog (Anthropic ADOPT sweep 2026-07) — Claude Code >=2.1.187 sandbox.credentials, schema verified against the 2.1.202 binary (files[].mode is literal 'deny'; envVars[].mode is 'deny'|'mask'; allowPlaintextInject optional, defaults false). Denies sandboxed Bash commands access to credential FILES (the subprocess-read class the permissions.deny Read() rail explicitly cannot cover — see _deny_baseline_comment) and unsets secret ENV VARS for sandboxed commands. INERT until sandbox.enabled=true (same flip discipline as the rest of this block). Honest limits: (1) this rail is HARNESS-side fail-open — the 2.1.202 loader drops an invalid entry or the whole block with a warning ('no credential protection is applied until it is fixed'), so the hook-side fail-CLOSED credential-leak guard in check_bash_safety.py remains the primary rail and this is defense-in-depth; (2) files paths resolve like sandbox.filesystem.* (absolute, ~ expanded, or relative to the project root) with NO glob support — the .env entries cover the repo ROOT only; subdir dotenv reads stay owned by the Read() deny rail + contamination CI; (3) envVars deliberately EXCLUDES GH_TOKEN/GITHUB_TOKEN/ANTHROPIC_API_KEY/OPENAI_API_KEY because gh, the `claude -p` eval harnesses, and the codex pair-rail all run through sandboxed Bash and may legitimately consume them — tighten only after an Owner-run probe (WATCH in docs/substrate-adopt-2026-07.md); (4) 'mask' mode (sentinel-in-sandbox + proxy inject on egress) is deliberately unused: it rests on egress-proxy TLS assumptions we have not probed; allowPlaintextInject stays explicit false.",
.claude/settings.json:147:        "_comment": "Bash safety: shlex-based parser replaces 5 substring-matching rules that false-positived on quoted strings during Sprint 2. Blocks: rm -rf (all flag combos), git reset --hard, git push --force/-f. Allows: --force-with-lease, quoted strings, compound commands with safe clauses. See check_bash_safety.py docstring for full logic.",
.claude/settings.json:152:            "command": "bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/_python-hook.sh\" check_bash_safety.py",
.claude/settings.json:231:        "_comment": "Arbitration-kernel HARD-DENY (PLAN-019 P1-SEC-A + PLAN-065 Layer A 2026-05-04): blocks Edit|Write|MultiEdit AND any mcp__* tool with write-shaped params on the hooks that enforce governance themselves + _lib policy/redact/audit-emit/contract primitives + .claude/policies. NO sentinel escape — only CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE=<reason-slug> + CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE_ACK=I-ACCEPT bypasses (bypass emits veto_triggered audit event with reason_code=kernel_override_used). Layer A closes S81-tris gap on kernel-protected paths.",
.claude/settings.json:279:        "_comment": "PLAN-075 v1.13.x narrow-promotion (ADR-106 + ADR-110): PreToolUse Pair-Rail Multi-LLM hook. When Edit|Write|MultiEdit targets an L3+ canonical-guarded path, invokes Codex MCP in read-only review mode and validates the response contains no write-shaped patches (apply_patch envelope, unified diff, JSON Patch RFC 6902). On Codex unavailable: fail-OPEN + breadcrumb. On write-shaped response: BLOCK + audit pair_rail_codex_violation. On clean review: ALLOW + audit pair_rail_review_passed. Sentinel-bypass short-circuits to ALLOW + audit pair_rail_sentinel_bypass. Kill-switches: CEO_PAIR_RAIL_DISABLE=1, CEO_PAIR_RAIL_TIMEOUT_S (default 180s; registration cap 210s — ADR-110-AMEND-2 recalibration, invariant guarded by test_pair_rail_timeout_invariant.py).",
.claude/settings.json:583:        "_comment": "PLAN-179 W1-b [amendment r1-C3]: Constraint Pinning PRIMARY channel. On a post-compaction session start (matcher 'compact' — the hook ALSO re-checks source == 'compact' in-process, never trusting the matcher alone), re-states the pinned governance constraints from the CODE constant _lib/pinned_constraints.PINNED_CONSTRAINTS (r1-C5 — never read from a .md at runtime, so it cannot be evicted by the summarizer) via additionalContext. RULES, not pointers: the PostCompact reinject hook is the REINFORCEMENT channel, this is the primary one, so pinning does not depend on the still-open W0-1 PostCompact channel verdict. ADVISORY, fail-OPEN, never blocks; emits NO audit event (the action is not yet in _KNOWN_ACTIONS — registration is a follow-up ceremony). Kill-switch: CEO_CONSTRAINT_PINNING=0 (deliberately NOT the shared CEO_COMPACTION_CONTINUITY — PLAN-179 §8.8: turning off the continuity snapshot must not silently disarm the governance floor).",
.claude/settings.json:814:  "_deny_baseline_comment": "PLAN-153 Wave E item 3 — coarse harness-level deny baseline (docs/deny-baseline.md). Entries 5-24 of permissions.deny below mirror scripts/install.sh DENY_BASELINE_ENTRIES exactly: credential-store reads (~/.ssh, ~/.aws, npm/gcloud/kube/docker/git-credentials/netrc/pypirc), dotenv-family reads (SPECIFIC .env variants only — a deny rule cannot carry allow exceptions, so .env.example/.sample/.template stay readable by omission; unlisted variants like .env.secret pass this backstop), and the curl|bash tripwire. Honest limits: Read deny does not cover arbitrary subprocesses opening files, Bash(curl * | bash) is bypassable by rephrasing (that class is owned by check_bash_safety.py), and **/.env is cwd-anchored. Gate floor: check_harness_config.py DENY_BASELINE (4 entries — PLAN-161 C1 removed the three Write() twins: on current CLIs (>=2.1.216) Edit(X) deny rules cover ALL file-editing tools and Write(X) rules are unconsulted; the Owner accepted the old-CLI residual) must remain a subset of this list.",
.claude/settings.json:817:  "_night_mode_deny_surface_comment": "PLAN-165 P1-corrected (D2 + round-2 findings NM-01/NM-03 + codex CX-1, Owner-ratified OQ1-redo 2026-08-03) — under defaultMode=acceptEdits a tool Edit/Write is auto-accepted, so every file that can DECIDE the next session's posture is deny-listed: (1) .claude/settings.local.json — the per-machine posture overlay (gitignored); a tool write of it is the direct escalation ladder. (2) .claude/state/night-mode.json — the night-mode marker/snapshot: night-mode off restores marker.prev_value into the overlay, so a marker write is a posture write BY PROXY (NM-01). (3) .claude/scripts/night-mode.py — the single sanctioned writer (NM-03). HONEST SCOPE (CX-1): these per-TOOL deny entries close only the Edit/Write rail — deny cannot see Bash. The load-bearing rail for Bash is _CANONICAL_GUARDS in check_canonical_edit.py (all three paths added there in the SAME ceremony; check_bash_safety keys off that list), plus kernel-tier listing of the two STATE files in check_arbitration_kernel.py. night-mode.py writes the overlay and the marker as a PROCESS (tempfile + os.replace), never via tools, so none of this costs a legitimate path — and per the Owner-ratified OQ1-redo, model-rail invocation of the toggle is itself blocked: on/off are HUMAN actions (terminal or the `!` prefix). The Write() twins were REMOVED in S292: the current harness (>=2.1.216) does NOT consult Write(path) rules in its file-permission check (the CLI emits an active warning for such rules) and the Edit(path) entries cover ALL file-editing tools — the same class PLAN-161 C1 removed from the credential-read baseline; the old-CLI residual documented there is now accepted for the posture files too, with the real defense on the _CANONICAL_GUARDS/kernel rails above (CX-1). Appended AFTER the curl|bash tripwire so entries 5-24 keep mirroring install.sh DENY_BASELINE_ENTRIES by position (see _deny_baseline_comment); these three entries are NOT part of that mirror. The three entries are byte-identical in templates/settings/settings.base.json (dogfood parity).",
